    known: ['The expedition needs ports that still function after capture.', 'Urban elites can open gates, delay, or transfer allegiance.', 'A reputation for terms is a military asset only if the army obeys them.'],
    caption: 'The route north depends upon political access as much as marching speed.',
    context: 'Sicily was taken rapidly. Naples resisted and was stormed after Roman troops entered through an unused aqueduct; Belisarius then moved to Rome, which the Goths abandoned in late 536.',
