    title: 'Two Commands, Three Objectives', role: 'Justinian - Master of rival victorious generals',
    question: 'How will Belisarius and Narses divide the Italian war?',
    brief: 'Rome has held, but the campaign now pulls north toward Milan, Auximum, and Ravenna. Belisarius and Narses disagree about concentration and the order of objectives. Rival access to the emperor can turn operational debate into institutional paralysis.',
